preConditionHook:
// THE SESSION'S MOVE HAS EXHAUSTED THE DAY'S RANGE. The distance travelled
// from the session's opening price to the current close has reached rangeFraction of the
// mean daily range of the last dailyLookback completed sessions, so there is
// little room left in the day and countertrend setups are favoured. INTRADAY
// ONLY -- on a daily or 1440-minute series the session is one bar and the test
// degenerates to |close - open| against the average range.
//
// Not OpeningRangeVsAvgDailyRange, which measures the HEIGHT OF THE OPENING
// RANGE against the same average and says what KIND of day it is; this measures
// how far the day has already gone and says the day is nearly done. Not
// AvgDailyRangeFractionStop, which is an Exit sizing a stop off the same
// average. All three inline the AverageDailyRange block for the value, as that
// rule's row says they do.
//
// THE SCAN is AverageDailyRange's, unchanged: walk back from bar 1, skip every
// bar carrying the CURRENT date so today's incomplete session never enters the
// average, open a day group on the first bar of a new date and close it when
// bar kk is the oldest bar of its date, day_of(Time(kk + 1)) != day_of(Time(kk))
// -- the read that makes the deepest index maxScanBars + 1. The dailyLookback
// guard WRAPS the date read rather than being ANDed with it, because
// EasyLanguage does not short-circuit and nesting is the only spelling in which
// a finished scan touches no further history in both twins. HighD/LowD/OpenD
// are VERIFIED but have no engine counterpart, so both twins scan bars and stay
// structurally identical.
//
// THE SESSION'S OPENING PRICE rides the same loop: a bar whose date IS the current date
// belongs to today, and because kk ascends the LAST such assignment is the
// OLDEST bar of today -- the session's first bar. sOpen is seeded with this
// bar's own open so the session's first bar reads its own open and the value is
// never stale.
//
// maxScanBars MUST COVER dailyLookback SESSIONS OF BARS and Max Bars Back must
// cover maxScanBars + 1. If the scan runs out first, adrDays stays short,
// adrReady is false and the rule is silent rather than wrong.
//
// Direction-agnostic (the move is measured with std::fabs, EL's AbsValue), so
// both sides are identical text. Every scratch value is a localVariables entry,
// never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
sOpen = open[0];
adrSum = 0.0;
adrDays = 0;
dHi = 0.0;
dLo = 0.0;
dOpen = false;
for (kk = 1; kk <= (int)maxScanBars; ++kk) {
    if (el_lt((double)adrDays, dailyLookback)) {
        if (day_of(ctx.Time(kk)) != day_of(ctx.Time(0))) {
            if (!dOpen) {
                dHi = high[kk];
                dLo = low[kk];
                dOpen = true;
            } else {
                if (el_gt(high[kk], dHi)) dHi = high[kk];
                if (el_lt(low[kk], dLo)) dLo = low[kk];
            }
            if (day_of(ctx.Time(kk + 1)) != day_of(ctx.Time(kk))) {
                adrSum = adrSum + (dHi - dLo);
                adrDays = adrDays + 1;
                dOpen = false;
            }
        } else {
            sOpen = open[kk];
        }
    }
}
adrReady = el_ge((double)adrDays, dailyLookback);
if (adrReady) {
    adr = adrSum / dailyLookback;
} else {
    adr = 0.0;
}
